{"format":1,"seq":835,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should improve how method suggestions rank: when a leaf like \"pr\" doesn't exist, I want to prioritize prefix matches within the same namespace (pr Create, prList, prView, prMerge) rather than alphabetical truncation that hides relevant results. I'm writing the logic to sort these prefix matches first.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01M4pBBB9jYoFhYXm1XNL8Ax","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Suggest same-namespace prefix matches first in injection hints\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { edit } }, p: { c: string }) => edit(\"src/sandbox/injection-hints.ts\", { revision: \"7D9K3THy_WqL\", changes: [{ kind: \"replace\", start: \"125:iooZU\", end: \"133:R6aG9\", content: p.c }] })","params":{"c":"  // A truncated method name, such as gh.pr for gh.prCreate, names the methods that extend it\n  // ahead of near misses elsewhere (#379).\n  const extensions = namespaces.includes(namespace)\n    ? names.filter(\n        (id) =>\n          id.startsWith(`${namespace}.${leaf}`) && !id.slice(namespace.length + 1).includes(\".\"),\n      )\n    : [];\n  const near = candidates\n    .map((id) => {\n      const idLeaf = id.slice(id.lastIndexOf(\".\") + 1);\n      return { id, distance: Math.min(editDistance(name, id), editDistance(leaf, idLeaf)) };\n    })\n    .filter((candidate) => candidate.distance <= threshold && !extensions.includes(candidate.id))\n    .sort((a, b) => a.distance - b.distance || a.id.localeCompare(b.id))\n    .map((candidate) => candidate.id);\n  const ranked = [...extensions.slice(0, MAX_LISTED_METHODS), ...near].slice(\n    0,\n    Math.max(MAX_SUGGESTIONS, Math.min(extensions.length, MAX_LISTED_METHODS)),\n  );"}}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01QwdGDcTU9Pk8uJ1qRimUe4","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Find injection hint tests\"}\nasync